    docTitle: "📄 Hygiene rules for gelato production",
    docHint: "Rules for preventing bacteria in artisan gelato production — available in Italian and German.",
    testimonialsTitle: "📬 What gelato makers write to us",
    testimonialsQuote: "\"Easy to use, really well made — finally a place to find everything you need in the artisan gelato business. The information request feature really works.\"",
    testimonialsNote: "We get a lot of messages with compliments and suggestions to improve the site, as well as requests from people who'd like to exchange links with us.",
    faqTitle: "❓ Frequently asked questions",
    faq2Q: "How can I compare two gelato bases from different companies?",
    faq2A: "In the Compare section of this site you can choose a product category and compare a Base product against two alternatives (A and B): the system shows company, technical specs and your personal ratings side by side, so you can see the real differences between products at a glance instead of relying only on commercial descriptions.",
    faq5Q: "What's the technical difference between a base 50 and a base 100?",
    faq5A: "The number indicates the recommended dosage in grams per liter of liquid. A base 50 requires more input from the gelato maker (sugars, milk solids) and offers more control over the final recipe; a base 100 is more structured and already balanced, so simpler to use but with less room for customization.",
    faq6Q: "Can I request information from manufacturers through the site?",
    faq6A: "Yes: in the Archive, next to each product, you'll find the \"Request information\" button: you fill in a form with your details and the request is forwarded directly to the manufacturer of the selected product.",
    faq7Q: "Is the site and its comparison tools free?",
    faq7A: "Yes, access to the database, product comparison and calibration tools is completely free and requires no registration: the site is designed as an independent, neutral platform that doesn't sell raw materials but provides technical data.",
